# 21. Frontend Functionality

Before visual redesign, verify real functionality:

- Data source
- API contract
- Loading
- Empty
- Error
- Permission state
- Disabled state
- Running state
- Success
- Failure
- Refresh
- Persistence
- Hard refresh
- Direct navigation
- Network behavior
- Console behavior
- i18n
- RTL
- Accessibility

Do not redesign around fake, placeholder or contradictory data.

No button may silently do nothing.

Disabled controls require a visible or accessible reason.

Unsupported capabilities must be truthful.

---

# 22. UI/UX and Design System

Every worked-on outcome must receive a UX review before closure.

Review:

- Information hierarchy
- Workflow clarity
- Primary action
- Secondary actions
- Status communication
- Capability communication
- Layout
- Cards
- Typography
- Spacing
- Forms
- Tables
- Loading
- Empty
- Error
- Disabled
- Confirmation
- Feedback
- Responsive layout
- Accessibility
- Keyboard
- Focus
- Dark theme
- i18n
- RTL
- Overflow
- Truncation

Redesign must improve usefulness, not merely appearance.

Remove unnecessary controls and complexity.

Do not preserve confusing UI solely because it exists.

## Canonical Design-System Source of Truth

Canonical reference:

`/home/ubuntu/webapp/TitanGold/DESIGN_SYSTEM_DATAHUB.md`

Primary reference implementation:

`components/ai/AIManager/tabs/DataHub/TelegramPanel.tsx`

Reuse existing shared tokens and components where applicable.

Do not create:

- A second color system
- Parallel button styles
- Parallel badge styles
- Parallel card tokens
- Parallel form styles
- Parallel modal patterns
- Another independent design-system utility layer

Adapt the design language to the workflow.

Do not copy business layout blindly.

